**Return exit code 2 for an invalid repository argument (src/selfhost/observe-prs.ts:15, 58).** When `GITHUB_REPOSITORY` is empty or malformed, `observeRepository` throws `invalid repository` at Line 15. The catch block at Line 58 maps every thrown error to exit code 1. Doctrine I1 defines exit 1 as a thrown error and exit 2 as an argument error. The `enterWithCqEnv` path at Line 46 already uses exit 2 for bad configuration. A misconfigured repository value therefore exits differently from a misconfigured CQ_* value. Callers cannot tell a usage error from a runtime failure.

Throw a dedicated usage error at Line 15 and map it to exit 2 in the catch block.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
+class UsageError extends Error {}
+
 export async function observeRepository(
@@
-  if (extra.length || !ghNameOk(owner) || !ghNameOk(repo)) throw new Error('invalid repository');
+  if (extra.length || !ghNameOk(owner) || !ghNameOk(repo)) throw new UsageError('invalid repository');
@@
     console.error(error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error));
-    process.exitCode = 1;
+    process.exitCode = error instanceof UsageError ? 2 : 1;
```
</details>





As per coding guidelines: "I1 ... Exit codes: 0 clean, 1 thrown error, 2 arg error, 3 needs-human."


Also applies to: 58-58
